# Phase 5: Payment Service, Redis Rate Limiting & Observability

## Goal

Add three production-critical capabilities to Service On Wheels:
1. **Payment Service** — Razorpay-based payment flow triggered after service completion
2. **Redis-backed Rate Limiting** — Replace the in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap` with Redis so rate limits survive restarts and scale across instances
3. **Observability Stack** — Prometheus metrics, Grafana dashboards, and Sentry error tracking

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Payment Gateway Choice**: This plan uses **Razorpay** (India's most popular gateway, free test mode, INR-native). If you prefer Stripe or another provider, let me know before I start.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Razorpay API Keys**: You'll need to create a free Razorpay test account at [dashboard.razorpay.com](https://dashboard.razorpay.com) to get `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` and `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`. The code will work with test keys — no real charges.

> [!WARNING]
> **Sentry DSN**: Sentry requires a project DSN (free tier at [sentry.io](https://sentry.io)). If you don't want to create a Sentry account right now, I can make it optional — the app will work fine without it, just with console-based error logging instead.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> **Pricing Model**: Should service charges be a flat rate per issue type (e.g., Flat Tire ₹500, Engine ₹1500), or dynamically calculated based on distance + service time? **This plan uses a flat-rate pricing table per issue type** since it's simpler and more predictable. Let me know if you want distance-based pricing instead.

